:1 + ]. In Hexateuch rarely P, 5:1 ; 14:35 ; Exod 16:22 ; J, Gen 3:11 ; 12:18 ; Exod 13:8 18 t.; E, Gen 21:6 ; 31:20 ; 41:25 15 t.; D, Deut 17:9 ; 26:3 ; 30:18 5 t.; — 1 tell, announce, report , usually human subject Gen 9:22 ; 24:23 ; 32:6 ; Lev 14:35 ; Judg 13:6 ; 1Sam 3:18 ; 1Kin 1:23 ; Neh 2:12 ; Est 2:10 (twice in verse); Job 12:7 ; Psa 142:3 ; Isa 19:12 ; Jer 5:20 ; Ezek 24:19 +. 2 declare, make known, expound , especially of something before not understood, concealed or mysterious, Gen 3:11 ; 12:18 , etc.; 1Kin 10:3 2Chr 9:2 ; a riddle Judg 14:12 , 15 , 16 (3 t. in verse); 14:19 ; dream Dan 2:2 ; secret Job 11:6 , etc.; of ׳י as revealing, Gen 41:25 ; 2Sam 7:11 ; 2Kin 4:27 ; Micah 6:8 ; Jer 42:3 ; Psa 147:19 ; of declaring by ׳י s agents Deut 5:5 ; Micah 3:8 ; 1Sam 15:16 ; 2Sam 24:13 ; Jer 50:28 ; Isa 58:1 ; by divin. Hosea 4:12 . 3 inform of (play the informer concerning) Josh 2:14 , 20 ; Jer 20:10 ; Job 17:5 ; Lev 5:1 ; Prov 29:24 . 4 publish declare, proclaim , especially of proclaiming wisdom, power, loving-kindness, etc., of ׳י (especially Psalms): Psa 9:12 ; Psalm 22:32; 51:17 ; 92:3 ; Psalm 92:16; 145:4 +, subject heavens 19:2 ; 50:6 ; 97:6 ; Isa 42:12 ; 57:12 . 5 avow, acknowledge, confess: Isa 3:9 ; Psa 38:19 , compare Isa 48:6 . &#8212; Participle = messenger 2Sam 15:13 ; Jer 51:31 (twice in verse) compare הַמַּגִּיד הַנַּ֫עַר 2Sam 1:5-6 , 13 ; הַמּ ׳הָאִישׁ 18:11 . Hoph`al Perfect הֻגַּד Josh 9:24 +; Imperfect וַיֻּגַּד Gen 22:20 +; Infinitive absolute הֻגֵּד Josh 9:24 ; Ruth 2:11 ; &#8212; be told, announced, reported , always followed by לְ (sometimes impersonal, logical subject in accusative, compare Gen 27:42 ; 2Sam 21:11 , with feminine Isa 21:2 ; not in P): Gen 27:42 (J), 31:22 (E), Deut 17:4 ; Josh 9:24 (twice in verse) (D), Ruth 2:11 (twice in verse); Judg 9:25 ; 2Sam 10:17 ; 19:2 ; 21:11 ; 1Kin 10:7 ; 18:13 ; 1Chr 19:17 ; 2Chr 9:6 ; Isa 21:2 ; 40:21 ; followed by לֵאמֹר Gen 22:20 ; 38:13 ; Genesis 13:24 (all J), Josh 10:17 (JE), 1Sam 15:12 